The forgotten ungroup()

trial |&gt;
  group_by(arm, sex) |&gt;
  summarise(n = n(), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
  mutate(pct = round(100 * n / sum(n), 1))

# A tibble: 4 x 4
  arm       sex       n   pct
  &lt;chr&gt;     &lt;chr&gt; &lt;int&gt; &lt;dbl&gt;
1 Placebo   F        15  25  
2 Placebo   M        15  25  
3 Treatment F        17  28.3
4 Treatment M        13  21.7









.groups = "drop" in summarise(), or ungroup() on the next line. Pick one and use it every time you group by more than one variable.

Grouped mutate() — the thing aggregate() cannot do

trial |&gt;
  group_by(arm) |&gt;
  mutate(sbp_0_centred = round(sbp_0 - mean(sbp_0), 1)) |&gt;
  ungroup() |&gt;
  select(id, arm, sbp_0, sbp_0_centred) |&gt; head(3)

# A tibble: 3 x 4
  id    arm     sbp_0 sbp_0_centred
  &lt;chr&gt; &lt;chr&gt;   &lt;dbl&gt;         &lt;dbl&gt;
1 P001  Placebo   160           9.8
2 P002  Placebo   162          11.8
3 P003  Placebo   157           6.8




Sixty rows out, not two. The group mean is computed per arm and recycled back across every row in that arm.

Translate the contract before the syntax
Before opening Python, state the R analysis in language-neutral terms:

one row represents one participant-visit;
retain week-4 rows;
keep missing outcomes available for the total denominator;
summarize within randomized arm;
return total n, observed n, mean, and SD.

Equivalent analyses need an explicit comparison
Compare at least:

input dimensions and key uniqueness;
rows retained by the analysis rule;
group labels and group sizes;
missing-value counts;
one or more numerical estimates within a stated tolerance;
output row and column meanings.

Matching printed tables is not enough if the two programs reached them through different populations.

Use AI as translation support, not authority
Copilot is now permitted under the Session 9 policy. When translating:

state the intended R semantics;
inspect indexing and missing-value defaults;
compare row counts and one numerical result;
disclose substantive assistance.

Do not ask AI to translate restricted data or confidential source.
